A builtin called with more arguments than its published signature
accepts (diag.builtin_excess_arguments, warning, ranged on the surplus
arguments): Left with three, Today with one. Skipped arguments count; a
call whose first surplus slot is skipped ranges on the name.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Clip;
	:PARAMETERS sText, nExtra, nA, nB;
	:DECLARE sOut, dNow;
	sOut := Left(sText, 10, nExtra);
	dNow := Today(1);
	sOut := Left(sText, nA, nB,,);
	sOut := Upper(sText,, nA);
	:RETURN sOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
